    "limits": {
      "macos": "Ad-hoc signed. The pinned install script extracts Sail.app into ~/Applications by default and attempts to strip quarantine. The archive updater selects the architecture-specific ZIP, including arm64 under Rosetta, and checks its SHA-512 and size. DMGs are manual install media. Updating requires access to replace the existing app bundle.",
      "linux": "Packaged in-app update requires AppImage or the .deb package. The shell desktop installer uses AppImage. The .deb update requires package installation privileges and may need a usable password prompt.",
      "cli": "install.sh uses SHA256SUMS and selects the platform archive. This release publishes Linux x64 and arm64 archives. No standalone macOS or Windows archive is published. The desktop shell script installs sail, separately from the standalone t3 CLI.",
      "policy": "Desktop update availability depends on the configured feed, production packaging, managed policy and T3CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_UPDATE.",
      "fly": "The Fly deployment uses the published OCI image. Upgrading is a redeploy with the existing volume. Source docs describe a possible brief disconnection.",
      "unpublished": "No Windows binary, native mobile build, separate web bundle, or WASM client release asset appears in this release. Upstream T3 Code distribution instructions do not establish Sail distribution."
    },
